{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805668-plot-help-strix-attracting-icon","id":805668,"title":"Plot Help: Strix attracting Icon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T18:29:01-08:00","id":805668,"title":"Plot Help: Strix attracting Icon","content":"So, I'm trying to tie together a plot thread, and while I have most of the middle details and the end, I'm kinda hazy of the source details.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm looking to make an Icon/Relic/Whatever that was created pre-1900, which when &quot;activated&quot; draws Strix to it, or causes them to appear. Maybe it opens up a gate to their shaowly home (thus &quot;spawning&quot; Strix), maybe they are interested in it and flock to it of their own volition, maybe it was made to compel them to come to it.<br /> <br /> My questions are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Who (as a group or individual) would be fitting as the maker of the thing.</li> <li>Why might they have made it (this is ultimately less important to the plot, but might help with Investigation, or splinter plot hooks).</li> </ol><br /> I lack the in depth lore to pick a fitting group. I'd rather not have to invent something else whole cloth if it can be helped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:42:13-08:00","id":806007,"title":"","content":"Could be a mage. If the Strix realm really is a Lower Depth they could have been trying to explore it or something.<br /> <br /> Actually even if it's not, they could have been trying under the assumption it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:48:09-08:00","id":806036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805668-plot-help-strix-attracting-icon?p=806007#post806007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be a mage. If the Strix realm really is a Lower Depth they could have been trying to explore it or something.<br /> <br /> Actually even if it's not, they could have been trying under the assumption it was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What would be a good thematic Mage group for that time period (&lt; 1900 CE), then? Does this seem up the alley for any Legacy or organization?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:51:38-08:00","id":806038,"title":"","content":"Probably one of the dodgier ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:31:43-08:00","id":806065,"title":"","content":"Not sure about your campaign setting or themes, but:<ul><li>Relic: Scales of Justice / Feather of Truth</li> <li>Creators: Followers of Seth (hunters / killers of Strix)</li> <li>Original Function: Protective / Exorcism</li> </ul><br /> At one time, the <i>feather of truth</i> was a process for the Followers of Seth to forcefully draw out a possessing Strix from the body of its victim. A white owl's feather would be placed on one side of an Egyptian balance-scale, while the freshly removed heart of an animal is placed on the other. Incantations of prayers and purity are spoken over the heart until it and the feather are in balance. This balance is maddening to the Strix in its presence. When the madness becomes too much to take, the Strix abandons its host in an effort to inhabit the ritual heart so that it again weighs more than the feather. When this is complete, the heart is placed in the mouth of its carcass. The animal shifts to undeath, devouring its own organ. This traps the Strix inside the animal, which would then be sacrificed to banish the Strix back into the underworld or destroy it utterly.<br /> <br /> In the centuries and conflicts after its initial use, the Strix who knew of the relic understood its paramount threat. Eventually, the Owls (or their minions) were successful in tainting the feather and the scale, disrupting its original purpose. Now, when the relic is used - it manifests an entirely new Strix. These Owls claim to have been newly made - or newly granted access to our world. It no longer has any effect on Strix in possession of a host, and in fact - those ridden by the Strix cannot activate the relic themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:40:05-08:00","id":806072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805668-plot-help-strix-attracting-icon?p=806065#post806065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about your campaign setting or themes, but:<ul><li>Relic: Scales of Justice / Feather of Truth</li> <li>Creators: Followers of Seth (hunters / killers of Strix)</li> <li>Original Function: Protective / Exorcism</li> </ul>At one time, the <i>feather of truth</i> was a process for the Followers of Seth to forcefully draw out a possessing Strix from the body of its victim. A white owl's feather would be placed on one side of an Egyptian balance-scale, while the freshly removed heart of an animal is placed on the other. Incantations of prayers and purity are spoken over the heart until it and the feather are in balance. This balance is maddening to the Strix in its presence. When the madness becomes too much to take, the Strix abandons its host in an effort to inhabit the ritual heart so that it again weighs more than the feather. When this is complete, the heart is placed in the mouth of its carcass. The animal shifts to undeath, devouring its own organ. This traps the Strix inside the animal, which would then be sacrificed to banish the Strix back into the underworld or destroy it utterly.<br /> <br /> In the centuries and conflicts after its initial use, the Strix who knew of the relic understood its paramount threat. Eventually, the Owls (or their minions) were successful in tainting the feather and the scale, disrupting its original purpose. Now, when the relic is used - it manifests an entirely new Strix. These Owls claim to have been newly made - or newly granted access to our world. It no longer has any effect on Strix in possession of a host, and in fact - those ridden by the Strix cannot activate the relic themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually would fit in with a possible Dark Eras setting in Ancient Egypt. And naturally in the possession of the Khaibit bloodline as part of their duties to the Great Covenant (mentioned in Ancient Bloodlines).<br /> <br /> And given some of the recent stuff I've been posting (conversions of the Bak-Ra and Usiri), it's only a matter of time before a Dark Eras setting gets thought up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:45:17-08:00","id":806076,"title":"","content":"Who could make it? Almost anyone. Strix are attracted to natural disasters, so the thing could just give off that kind of resonance, and naturally draw the Owls of Dis in. Its creation could be a mistake from the Ordo Dracul. Belial's brood worshipers could want this. Cruac ritual gone wrong. Some Theban Sorcerers messing around with forbidden magic creates it, trying to make something akin to the Shroud ritual. The Jaing Shi, some revenants, an old tired Strix wanting to take a nap inside a physical object for a few centuries. Hells, maybe its actually a connection to an elder vampire's mind, who's sleeping in the Strix realm, and the object just acts as a gateway to bring her back!<br /> <br /> Pretty much anyone could do it. We could help more with more plot details.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:25:11-08:00","id":806207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805668-plot-help-strix-attracting-icon?p=806065#post806065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the centuries and conflicts after its initial use, the Strix who knew of the relic understood its paramount threat. Eventually, the Owls (or their minions) were successful in tainting the feather and the scale, disrupting its original purpose. Now, when the relic is used - it manifests an entirely new Strix. These Owls claim to have been newly made - or newly granted access to our world. It no longer has any effect on Strix in possession of a host, and in fact - those ridden by the Strix cannot activate the relic themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit slower than desired, but this could be a useful source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805668-plot-help-strix-attracting-icon?p=806076#post806076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who could make it? Almost anyone. Strix are attracted to natural disasters, so the thing could just give off that kind of resonance, and naturally draw the Owls of Dis in. Its creation could be a mistake from the Ordo Dracul. Belial's brood worshipers could want this. Cruac ritual gone wrong. Some Theban Sorcerers messing around with forbidden magic creates it, trying to make something akin to the Shroud ritual. The Jaing Shi, some revenants, an old tired Strix wanting to take a nap inside a physical object for a few centuries. Hells, maybe its actually a connection to an elder vampire's mind, who's sleeping in the Strix realm, and the object just acts as a gateway to bring her back!<br /> <br /> Pretty much anyone could do it. We could help more with more plot details.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pertinent details:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Arrived in the US post World War I as a war souvenir/plunder. (Thus, needs to predate WWI)</li> <li>Activation can be triggered accidentally. (Such pouring blood on it, or some other uncommon, but possible trigger)</li> <li>When activated, the number of Strix in the area increases noticeably. (Either creating, summoning, or calling them)</li> </ol><br /> I'm aware I can pick just about anything. And I can even leave it a complete mystery. But I'm hoping giving it a more concrete origin will help with related details.<br /> <br /> Some plot events (high level):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Triggered accidentally, summons Strix, leaves domain decimated.</li> <li>Fall into the hands of a collector/researcher/occultist. Who starts researching the curiosity.</li> <li>Co-researcher becomes obsessed with it and triggers it accidental. More Strix, fewer vampires.</li> <li>Obsessed researcher banished. Get infected with something. Thinks Strix can cure him. Steals the Icon to summon them.</li> <li>Summons them. More *fun* for the domain. Researcher not cured (yet?). Vampires locate the source of their recurring owl problem.</li> <li>Icon gets sealed/banished for a time. (hard to destroy)</li> <li>Researcher find/acquires/unseals the Icon ahead of schedule.</li> <li>Cue Entry into the plot. (From here I have a few outlines regarding how things can fall out, depending on PC choices.)</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:51:33-08:00","id":806615,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think of the secret society known as the <a href=\"http://www.comicvine.com/court-of-owls/4060-58693/\" target=\"_blank\">Court of Owls</a>, as inspiration for a group the would seek to posses such an artifact.(Maybe it's one of their spooky masks) And remember, the world of CofD is larger and stranger than just Vampires, so a mysterious object of power could come from anywhere. &quot;The darkness only conceals more Darkness...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}